<title>USA: Clinton praises EU Boeing deal.</title>
<headline>Clinton praises EU Boeing deal.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton praised the European Union's resolution Wednesday of differences with Boeing over its merger with McDonnell Douglas.</p>
<p>&quot;I am pleased that Boeing and the EU have resolved their differences,&quot; Clinton said in a written statement.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope that the EU will give the merger final approval expeditiously.&quot;</p>
<p>In Brussels, European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert -- who announced the broad agreement with Boeing -- said he was confident of approval when the final decision is made next week.</p>
<p>Clinton said the merger &quot;will promote consolidation and efficiency in the U.S. defense industry and preserve the jobs of 14,000 workers at Douglas aircraft company.&quot;</p>
<p>In the past few days, Clinton and top members of his administration were in close contact with the Europeans urging them to reach agreement with Boeing.</p>
</text>
